      "id": 4383956251,
      "body": "Advancing an upstream task does not fence its existing receipt here. For example, after sealing CMAD1 at revision 1 and assigning CMAD1 revision 2, a currently authorized CMAD2 submission can still use the revision-1 predecessor: these checks only compare policy/epoch and artifact bytes, and neither discovery nor assignment advancement invalidates that receipt. This lets downstream stages seal against superseded task evidence. Check each ancestor's recorded principal/revision against its current host_tasks assignment before accepting it.",
