    {
      "id": 4383956285,
      "body": "Resolving the path here removes symlink components before the guarded reader can reject them. An artifact replaced by an in-scope symlink is rejected by `digest_file(original_path, root)`, but `source_changed` returns `True`; a dangling in-scope symlink also returns `True`. Consequently, reopening can accept these paths and persist invalidations despite the newly enforced symlink-denial policy. Pass the original path to the guarded reader and recognize missing-source drift only when its underlying failure is `FileNotFoundError`, preserving scope denials for symlinks.",
      "url": "https://github.com/CollaborativeMinD/HMT-RnD-Environment/pull/3#discussion_r4383956285",
